  "mapping_guidance": [
    "Treat scene units as metres, or apply explicit model-units-to-metres conversion.",
    "Repeat physical texture tile sizes from tile_size_m; for a planar face, repeat=(physical width/tile width,physical height/tile height).",
    "World-space/triplanar mapping avoids UV distortion, but orient timber grain and masonry manually to match construction.",
    "Only basecolor uses sRGB; roughness and normals are non-color data. RoughnessMap reads green channel in Three.js.",
    "All texture normal maps are OpenGL +Y. Use normalScale as a preview-tuned multiplier, not a measured height.",
    "No metallic maps are needed for these dielectric surfaces. Keep metalness=0. White painted steel is a separate painted dielectric material.",
    "Use separately authored smooth physical materials for glass, polished metal and painted steel, not these diffuse scans.",
    "Load only the materials used by a model. Do not eagerly load every variant or the entire library."
